////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
// alternate_base_fp_multiplier
// Review contract
- BASE is a power of two and at least 2; BASE_WIDTH = log2(BASE).
- EXPONENT_WIDTH is positive and MANTISSA_WIDTH >= BASE_WIDTH. Equality is supported.
- REGISTERED_IN and REGISTERED_NORMALIZE are 0 or 1. LUTX^GRADE must exceed 1,
  and all sticky-tree levels and padded groups must fit the existing SMALL/SOLAR map capacities.
- Inputs are canonical: exponent zero requires mantissa zero; other zero-exponent encodings are undefined.
- Every finite nonzero input has a nonzero leading radix digit. There is no implicit leading bit.
- The value is (-1)^sign * (mantissa / 2^MANTISSA_WIDTH) * BASE^(exponent - bias).
- Subnormal results flush to zero after rounding. The computed sign is retained, so both signed zeros exist.
- There is no reset or valid port; outputs are unspecified until valid samples fill the pipeline.
- NaN/Inf takes precedence over canonical zero: either special operand preserves the combined NaN/Inf class.
- A single pipelined bit preserves that class; the XOR sign and the other mantissa bits use the ordinary datapath.
