- round & (sticky | lsb) implements nearest-even: above-half values increment, and exact ties increment only odd mantissas.
- normalized_mantissa_round_p packs the retained mantissa above the round bit.
- Clear the M+1-bit accumulator, copy only the retained M bits into its low M positions, then add increment.
- Bit M of normalized_rounded is the carry slot, initialized to zero before addition.
- A rounding carry clears the low M bits; insert the shifted carry at POST_NORMALIZE_CARRY_INDEX and increment the exponent.
- The M+1-bit accumulator retains the carry. Adding the unsigned one-bit increment adds zero or one, not a replicated mask.
- Only the lower M retained bits become zero on carry; the carry bit itself is one.
- OR the carry into bit MANTISSA_WIDTH-BASE_WIDTH, not necessarily the mantissa MSB. The exponent rises by one radix unit.
- The zero flag suppresses the exponent increment for a zero operand.
