////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
// Baseline input-special propagation before the special-over-zero priority revision - 11/05/26
- WSL Verilator 5.048: 6,902 exact-integer reference vectors across four register settings,
  totaling 27,608 transactions in 40 parameter/register combinations.
- Ten parameter sets cover BASE 2/4/8/16/256; mantissa widths 1/2/4/5/6/12/24/64;
  exponent widths 2/3/4/5/32/33; LUTX 4/6; GRADE 1/2; and sticky latency 0/1/2.
- Checked outputs, the unchanged arithmetic overflow/underflow flags, and inf_nan_operand_p before
  and after clock edges against an independent Python arbitrary-precision integer model.
- Signed-zero signs are compared, not discarded. The existing LATENCY is checked independently for every configuration.
- Covered both normalization choices, above/below-half rounding, even/odd ties, rounding carry,
  exponent-zero flush, both overflow classes, finite maximum-exponent results, and range rescues
  caused by normalization or rounding carry. Canonical zero times NaN/Inf is checked in both operand orders.
- Covered special operands on either side, both operands special, all sign combinations, special/finite/zero
  transitions, and finite maximum-exponent inputs with mantissa MSB zero that must not set the input flag.
- 1,419 nonzero-special vectors would otherwise have produced a finite ordinary result; all retain the reserved class.
- Questa 2025.2: compilation succeeded and 13 directed cases passed under the previous zero-first policy.
- Invalid MANTISSA_WIDTH=3 with BASE=16 was rejected by the existing time-zero fatal assertion.
- All 27 current quoted RTL/package excerpts were checked against the source files.

////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
// NaN/Inf-over-zero priority re-verification - 11/05/26
- Only the final priority order changed; arithmetic, sign generation, flag pipelines, and LATENCY are unchanged.
- WSL Verilator 5.048: 1,066 exact-integer reference vectors across all four register settings,
  totaling 4,264 transactions in 40 parameter/register combinations using the ten baseline parameter sets.
- Checked product_o, both ordinary range flags, inf_nan_operand_p, and zero_operand_p before and after clock edges.
- Included special times canonical zero in both operand orders, all four sign combinations, and multiple payloads;
  each result retains the maximum exponent and mantissa MSB one, with the existing XOR sign.
- Interleaved ordinary finite, ordinary zero, nonzero special, and special-plus-zero flag combinations to check alignment.
- Ordinary zero, finite underflow, finite overflow, maximum-exponent finite input, and rounding-carry controls passed.
- Questa 2025.2: 13 directed cases passed with the revised priority. Both metadata flags may be one together;
  the special branch is selected first, so zero cannot clear the reserved output encoding.
- All 27 source/helper excerpts match the current RTL/package. The adder already uses the same class-first policy.

////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
// Single-bit NaN/Inf propagation policy - 11/05/26
- Either input's maximum-exponent/mantissa-MSB encoding sets one bit after REGISTERED_IN selection.
- REGISTERED_NORMALIZE and the sticky-latency pipe carry that bit alongside the existing fields without extra cycles.
- At the output, the special bit takes priority over canonical zero and forces maximum exponent and mantissa MSB one.
- The XOR sign and computed lower mantissa bits are retained. A single flag preserves the combined class,
  without preserving an individual NaN payload or distinguishing NaN from Inf.
- The former 0x7800 times 0x1100 counterexample now produces reserved output 0x7800 instead of finite 0x4800.



